WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.360
Two models got the same score,

2
00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:05.600
but their mistakes told completely different stories.

3
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.620
28 fictional cases tested field normalization.

4
00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.830
Three model IDs produced 84 answers.

5
00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:18.400
Gemini scored 28. Claude and Gemma, 26.

6
00:00:21.113 --> 00:00:22.360
Explicit rules in.

7
00:00:22.597 --> 00:00:24.238
Raw responses out.

8
00:00:24.238 --> 00:00:27.100
Code checks JSON, status, and canonical value.

9
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.450
Native traces preserve each prompt and answer.

10
00:00:30.881 --> 00:00:34.721
Take the text 4.700.

11
00:00:34.721 --> 00:00:38.300
The declared Brazilian convention
makes that dot a thousands separator.

12
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.320
Claude called it ambiguous.

13
00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.760
Gemma returned the right amount, but
omitted the required decimal places.

14
00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:47.001
Both lost a strict point.

15
00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:55.500
After those results, we registered 12 new
money cases before collecting answers.

16
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.379
Same three model IDs. Two repetitions.

17
00:00:57.379 --> 00:01:01.860
72 responses, separate from the original 84.

18
00:01:03.678 --> 00:01:07.950
For 3.600, the source declares a decimal point.

19
00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:10.318
Claude abstained again.

20
00:01:10.318 --> 00:01:13.549
Gemma omitted a required zero in repetition one,

21
00:01:13.549 --> 00:01:15.839
then passed this case in repetition two.

22
00:01:21.177 --> 00:01:22.829
Gemini scored 12 twice.

23
00:01:22.829 --> 00:01:24.850
Claude scored 7, then 6.

24
00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.578
Gemma, 11, then 12.

25
00:01:27.578 --> 00:01:29.878
Claude had 7 unnecessary abstentions,

26
00:01:29.878 --> 00:01:33.458
3 JSON-container violations and 1 wrong amount.

27
00:01:33.458 --> 00:01:35.778
All 24 control responses passed.

28
00:01:37.276 --> 00:01:41.797
These targeted cases do not
establish general model superiority.

29
00:01:41.797 --> 00:01:44.090
Values and wording changed together.

30
00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:47.218
Inspect the raw answers and grading code.

31
00:01:47.218 --> 00:01:49.037
Same score. Different failure.
